{"title":"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2018 AMC 10A #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">2018 AMC 12A #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alice, Bob, and Charlie were on a hike and were wondering how far away the nearest town was. When Alice said, \"We are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles away,\" Bob replied, \"We are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles away.\" Charlie then remarked, \"Actually the nearest town is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles away.\" It turned out that none of the three statements were true. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the distance in miles to the nearest town. Which of the following intervals is the set of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1ac07bf6394983fd2b652c65343f073acbc7e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }   (0,4)   \\qquad        \\textbf{(B) }   (4,5)   \\qquad    \\textbf{(C) }   (4,6)   \\qquad   \\textbf{(D) }  (5,6)  \\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }   (5,\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"517\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each of the false statements, we identify its corresponding true statement. Note that:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe6dc48b595a2cadc50a15f4d6c23701ae43c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{False}\\cap\\mathrm{True}=\\varnothing.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e4d1151fb5b5583e177d288c8e032803a410eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{False}\\cup\\mathrm{True}=[0,\\infty).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>We construct the following table:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1645d4ff8df04a7bdc85c3c64aac7453f53711a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c||c|c} &amp; &amp;  \\\\ [-2.5ex] \\textbf{Hiker} &amp; \\textbf{False Statement} &amp; \\textbf{True Statement} \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\textbf{Alice} &amp; [6,\\infty) &amp; [0,6) \\\\  &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2.25ex] \\textbf{Bob} &amp; [0,5] &amp; (5,\\infty)  \\\\ &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2.25ex] \\textbf{Charlie} &amp; [0,4] &amp; (4,\\infty) \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"99\" />\nTaking the intersection of the true statements, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e8ff50fd0dbecfbb52f8742566d5fd1241f893.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[0,6)\\cap(5,\\infty)\\cap(4,\\infty)=(5,6)\\cap(4,\\infty)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } (5,6)}.\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"30\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Think of the distances as if they are on a number line. Alice claims that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0cbca851f5bc206fcf12525b35af8ae98c53d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &gt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, Bob says <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b43ad1bb1ad72a0e1c7166b276d28421a8d3ef24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, while Charlie thinks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c0e2600d06800097672d53f7d816c438cd248d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. This means that all possible numbers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are included. However, since the three statements are actually false, the distance to the nearest town is one of the numbers not covered. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/3978c6790fea080c150457b476ff05655f3cd7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } (5,6)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"88\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nNEXCxWLJzc\">https://youtu.be/nNEXCxWLJzc</a>\n</p><p>Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vO-ELYmgRI8\">https://youtu.be/vO-ELYmgRI8</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cLJ87xJzcWI\">https://youtu.be/cLJ87xJzcWI</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black